          "text": "Clinical Indication  \nHistory of generalized epilepsy with generalized tonic-clonic seizures beginning at age 38, occurring approximately twice per month. Etiology is unknown. Seizures are drug responsive. Current antiseizure medications are carbamazepine and levetiracetam.\n\nTechnique  \nRoutine scalp EEG recorded using the international 10–20 electrode placement system and reviewed in standard montages.\n\nFindings  \nNo authorized electrographic findings were provided; therefore, the background, interictal activity, and presence or absence of electrographic seizures cannot be characterized.\n\nImpression  \nIndeterminate routine EEG due to unavailable electrographic findings. No conclusions regarding epileptiform abnormalities or ictal localization can be made from the provided information.",
